msgstr ""

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_domains.md#L29
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_domains.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/trust_domains.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_domains.md:29
msgid "The Digital Documentation of COVID-19 Certificates (DDCC) published in August 2021 and similar guidance for test results (https://www.who.int/publications/i/item/WHO-2019-nCoV-Digitalcertificatesdiagnostictestresults-2022.1) published in March 2022 serve as the reference for the associated FHIR Implementation Guide. This Implementation Guide (IG) acts as the computable representation of the core data elements in the published guidance, mapped to standard terminologies. These data models, in the form of FHIR logical models, and terminologies, in the form of FHIR value sets, are the basis for interoperability between the various credential formats. The IG provides FHIR Structure Maps and Concept Maps to define transformations between supported credential formats and the core data set, which allows business rules to execute against a common set of data elements."
msgstr ""

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_domains.md#L13
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_domains.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/trust_domains.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_domains.md:13
msgid "The GDHCN Administrative and Operational Framework is the legal source for Trust Domains. The Trust Domain logical model follows its three-part definition: use cases (modelled by DAK components), technical specifications, and policy and regulatory standards. A Trust Domain also names its terms of use, which is a ValueSet of the policies a participant may say it acts under."
msgstr ""

#. Source: https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust/blob/main/input/pagecontent/trust_domains.md#L17
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust/trust_domains.html
#. URL: https://litlfred.github.io/smart-trust/trust_domains.html
#: input/pagecontent/trust_domains.md:17
msgid "The model allows each part to be empty, but an empty part is a QA error. So is a terms-of-use ValueSet that no BPMN business process uses."
msgstr ""

